                <pb facs="0263" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/517: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shea</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-27T19:00:00-04:42"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                                1919, 7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            October 28, 5.44 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Chilean Fleet has been ordered to the north ports. The press states that this
                    is not an offensive movement but is done out of an abundance of caution. This is
                    supplemental to my October 20, noon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Shea</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
